WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.935
-As the president
continues to lie

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:05.171
about the coronavirus outbreak,
we are now seeing

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.406
what it's like
when a lifelong scam artist

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.943
is in charge of responding
to a public health crisis.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:11.978
For more on this,
it's time for a closer look.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:16.716
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.384
When it comes to his presidency,

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.119
there's nothing Donald Trump
cares about more

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:21.420
than the stock market.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.522
He brags about it virtually
every chance he gets,

00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:26.759
and on Friday, during a visit
to CDC headquarters in Atlanta,

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.361
Trump predicted
that the coronavirus outbreak,

00:00:29.361 --> 00:00:32.498
which has now hit more than
100,000 cases worldwide

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:34.834
and over 500 here in the U.S.,

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.236
would actually be good
for the economy.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.472
-Could you just address the
economic piece, though,

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.841
because there's obviously a lot
of fear about the coronavirus?

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.776
-I mean it is a fact.
You know, if you don't want

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.545
to think about me,
I like when people happen

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.846
to stay in the United States

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.415
and spend their money
in the United States, okay?

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.751
So, I think people are staying
in the United States,

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.686
they're going to spend their
money in the United States.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.755
-That's right,
Trump thinks coronavirus

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.457
will help the economy
because people will

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.958
spend money here in the U.S.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.861
[ As Trump ] In fact, I've been
buying toilet paper at Costco

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:06.599
that I'm going to resell
at a profit if things get worse.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.300
There you go.
The president said on Friday

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.870
that coronavirus would actually
be good for the economy.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.672
Let's see
how the stock market did

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.507
when it opened
on Monday morning.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.176
-We're coming on the air
with breaking news.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.110
This is
the New York Stock Exchange.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.880
The trading day is just
beginning on Wall Street.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.983
And there are fears that the Dow
will drop and drop quickly,

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.551
and we're already seeing that.

00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:29.855
The Dow industrials are off
right now 17 points or 6.5%,

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:32.992
you've got the NASDAQ off 5.8%,

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:36.095
and then the S&amp;P down 6 1/3%.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.464
-At this point, I've never seen
this much anxiety

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.232
on the floor of
the New York Stock Exchange.

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:42.301
There are traders
running everywhere.

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:43.736
We are watching these levels.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:47.507
-Has trading now stopped?
Has it hit that 7% figure?

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:51.344
-Trading has stopped because
we've seen a drop of 7%,

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:55.014
which means trading will stop
for the next 15 minutes.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:58.283
-[ As Trump ] I'm selling this
toilet paper for $1,000 a sheet!

00:01:58.283 --> 00:02:01.387
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:05.024
[ Normal voice ]
That's right. Three days.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.525
Three days after Trump predicted

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:08.527
coronavirus would be good
for the economy,

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:10.563
the stock market plunged
so much, when it opened,

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.164
the trading had to be stopped.

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:15.134
The drop was so bad,
the red arrow on the TV screen

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:20.139
grew legs and ran away.

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:24.844
Now, the selloff wasn't due
entirely to coronavirus.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:27.980
It was also due in large part
to a war over oil prices

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.548
launched by Saudi Arabia.

00:02:29.548 --> 00:02:31.784
Still, a lot of people
are understandably worried.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.752
And while there's
no the reason to panic,

00:02:33.752 --> 00:02:35.988
governments across the world are
taking extreme measures

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:37.590
to mitigate the outbreak.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.126
Over the weekend, Italy put
millions of people on lockdown

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.928
in regions hit hardest
by the outbreak

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:44.330
where people were rushing
to catch the last trains

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.966
leaving Milan before
the lockdown took effect.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:50.169
-Officials in Italy putting
16 million people on lockdown.

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:52.972
Now, that's a quarter
of the country's population.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.408
Video shows people rushing
to catch the last train

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:57.309
as they left northern Italy.

00:02:57.309 --> 00:03:01.147
-This is what Italians look like
when they're rushing.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.917
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:08.621
I mean, obviously, in Italy,

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:11.924
to run for a train is
a fate worse than death.

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:14.627
I'm shocked they didn't have
cigarettes in one hand

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.930
and Aperol spritzers
in the other.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.231
I mean, if you've ever
been to Italy,

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.365
you know that, for Italians,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.933
what you just saw there
is DEFCON one.

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:23.402
I mean, in Italy, stores
just close in the afternoon

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:25.771
so people can nap,
and planes just take off

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.140
whenever they want.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.475
At the Rome airport,
most departure times say,

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.344
"It leaves when it leaves,
capiche?"

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:35.414
And here in the U.S., New York,
the state with the most cases,

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:37.516
is currently taking
its own precautions

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:39.118
to deal with the coronavirus.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.053
Governor Andrew Cuomo declared
a state of emergency

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:43.856
as the number of cases rises
to over 100

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:47.126
with thousands more being asked
to self-quarantine.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.295
And on Sunday,
Cuomo offered this advice

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.597
to New Yorkers taking
the subway.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:56.369
-If you can move to a train car
that is not as dense,

00:03:56.369 --> 00:04:00.973
if you see a packed train car,
let it go by.

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:03.141
Wait for the next train.

00:04:03.141 --> 00:04:04.410
-I'm sorry, did you think

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:08.180
people were picking crowded cars
on purpose?

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.817
Every train car is packed.

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:14.286
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:16.088
"Excuse me. I'm sorry.

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:19.224
Where are the less-dense
train cars?"

00:04:19.224 --> 00:04:21.794
That's why
those showtime subway dancers

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.996
learned to hang upside down
from the roof,

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:27.033
so they could fit
onto a packed car.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.468
As a general rule,
any time you see a subway car

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:31.337
that isn't packed,
that means one of two things --

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.006
either it's 4:00 a.m.
on a Tuesday

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:35.074
or someone did
something unspeakable.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.510
"Oh, look, honey.
This one's almost empt--

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.246
Oh, that smell. Oh, my God."

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:41.781
Now, there's no reason to panic.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:44.650
In fact, as bad as things seem,
there are reasons for optimism.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.787
China and South Korea have seen
slowdowns in new cases

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.522
and people in areas affected
by the outbreak

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:51.724
have been making the best
of the situation.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:54.560
For example, in Wuhan, China,
the epicenter of the outbreak,

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.296
students
who had been on lockdown

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.164
were assigned homework
through an app

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:00.433
until they figured out a way
to get out of it.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.568
In locked-down Wuhan,
teachers used an app

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.837
called DingTalk
to set up homework.

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:07.373
Kids realized if it got enough
one-star reviews,

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.341
it would be reviewed
from the app store.

00:05:09.341 --> 00:05:11.743
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thousands of reviews flooded in,

00:05:11.743 --> 00:05:16.549
and DingTalk's rating fell
from 4.9 to 1.4 overnight.

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:18.384
That is amazing.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.452
Although I will say,
although it is a bummer

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:21.921
for the people
who built that app.

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.856
I mean, you conceive of an app,
you develop it,

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.958
you go through rounds and rounds
of beta testing,

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:27.960
you finally have
a successful launch,

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.062
and then this brings it down.

00:05:30.062 --> 00:05:32.197
"Hey, what happened to that app
of yours?"

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:36.101
"A bunch of dickhead kids
one-starred me."

00:05:36.101 --> 00:05:40.739
"Well, you made a homework app,
so maybe you're the dickhead."

00:05:40.739 --> 00:05:43.575
But, honestly,
maybe we should put these kids

00:05:43.575 --> 00:05:45.477
in charge
of the coronavirus response.

00:05:45.477 --> 00:05:47.046
Because while they
were out there,

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.848
coming up with ways
to shut down apps,

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:50.415
the most powerful man
in the world was visiting

00:05:50.415 --> 00:05:53.852
CDC headquarters in Atlanta on
Friday in a hat and windbreaker

00:05:53.852 --> 00:05:57.323
looking, not like a man steady
at the helm of a crisis,

00:05:57.323 --> 00:06:00.059
but like a hung-over
little-league umpire.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:03.462
Seriously, man,
what is this look?

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:05.330
You are inside.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.466
Are you expecting
a thunderstorm?

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:09.801
[ As Trump ]
I heard there was a laboratory,

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:12.137
and as everyone knows,
laboratories run on lightning

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:15.040
because that's how
they invented Frankenstein."

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.109
[ Normal voice ] And as
countries across the world

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:19.278
were testing tens of thousands
of people a day

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:21.848
and taking extreme measures
to mitigate the outbreak,

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.749
our president was at the CDC
talking about

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:25.418
how he was getting
his information

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:28.921
not from doctors, but from his
favorite channel, Fox News.

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:31.457
-As of the time
I left the plane with you,

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:34.827
we had 240 cases,
or that's at least what was on

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:40.032
a very fine network
known as Fox News.

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:41.901
-Why are you getting
your information

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:44.971
about how many cases there are
from Fox News?

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:48.708
You're at the CDC.

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:53.379
You are surrounded -- You are
currently surrounded by doctors.

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:56.148
Just turn around
and ask one of them.

00:06:56.148 --> 00:06:57.249
Doctor, give it to me straight.

00:06:57.249 --> 00:06:59.185
Did you see me on Hannity
last night?

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:01.253
Was I good?

00:07:01.253 --> 00:07:03.356
Kind of terrifying that in
the middle of a global pandemic,

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:05.924
Trump is getting his information
from Fox News

00:07:05.924 --> 00:07:08.928
because at the same time Trump
is listening to Fox,

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:11.663
public health officials are
worried about making him angry

00:07:11.663 --> 00:07:13.231
by telling him the truth.

00:07:13.231 --> 00:07:15.201
For example, Politico reported
that public health groups

00:07:15.201 --> 00:07:17.837
are hoping to convey
factual information to Americans

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:19.572
without antagonizing Trump.

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:21.239
They're afraid
of antagonizing Trump.

00:07:21.239 --> 00:07:22.308
That is insane.

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:23.342
They're talking about
the president

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:25.043
the way a mailman
talks about a rottweiler

00:07:25.043 --> 00:07:27.980
which makes sense
because Trump always looks

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.716
like he's about to bite
an intruder on the ass.

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:33.185
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:33.185 --> 00:07:36.555
And you can tell
that the cult of personality

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:39.491
that insulates Trump
from dissent is having an impact

00:07:39.491 --> 00:07:42.028
because Trump appointees keep
going out of their way

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:44.830
to compliment him in situations
where it's totally unnecessary,

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.266
from the health secretary
to the head of the CDC

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:49.668
to the surgeon general
just yesterday on CNN.

00:07:49.668 --> 00:07:51.370
-Thank you, Mr. President,

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.472
for gathering your public health
experts here today

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:56.509
and for your strong leadership
in keeping America safe.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:58.577
-I want to thank you
for your decisive leadership

00:07:58.577 --> 00:08:01.747
in helping us
put public health first.

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:04.116
-We want to make sure folks
who are out there who at risk,

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:05.618
they're taking
extra precautions.

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:07.786
But speaking of being at risk,
the president,

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:10.590
he sleeps less than I do,
and he's healthier than I am.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:13.892
-No, he's not. There's no way
he's healthier than you are.

00:08:13.892 --> 00:08:14.927
I mean, look at him.

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:16.128
He doesn't even know
the difference

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:18.431
between inside and outside.

00:08:18.431 --> 00:08:20.099
I'd expect him to bring
an umbrella,

00:08:20.099 --> 00:08:23.302
but he doesn't know
how to use one.

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:27.072
Trump is desperately,
desperately trying to paint

00:08:27.072 --> 00:08:29.742
a rosy picture to help
both his political fortunes

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:32.445
and the economy, which he sees
as crucial to his reelection.

00:08:32.445 --> 00:08:34.813
For example, on Friday,
Trump actually admitted

00:08:34.813 --> 00:08:38.184
that he wanted to keep people
trapped on a cruise ship

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:41.020
where passengers and crews were
diagnosed with coronavirus

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.856
rather than bringing them
onto the U.S. mainland

00:08:43.856 --> 00:08:46.525
because it would increase
the number of coronavirus cases

00:08:46.525 --> 00:08:48.995
in the U.S., and that would
make him look bad.

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:52.464
-I mean, frankly, uh,
if it were up to me,

00:08:52.464 --> 00:08:55.601
I would be inclined to say
leave everybody on the ship

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:58.403
for a period of time
and use the ship as your base.

00:08:58.403 --> 00:09:01.774
But a lot of people would rather
do it a different way.

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:03.875
They'd rather quarantine people.

00:09:03.875 --> 00:09:05.144
And when they do that,

00:09:05.144 --> 00:09:07.245
our numbers are going to
go up, okay?

00:09:07.245 --> 00:09:08.714
Our numbers are going to go up.

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:10.049
They would like to have
the people come off.

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:11.550
I'd rather have the people stay.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:14.486
But I go with them. I told them
to make the final decision.

00:09:14.486 --> 00:09:16.288
I would rather
because I like the numbers

00:09:16.288 --> 00:09:17.856
being where they are.

00:09:17.856 --> 00:09:22.127
I don't need to have the numbers
double because of one ship.

00:09:22.127 --> 00:09:24.630
-I'm sorry, but keeping people
trapped on a cruise ship

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.164
even if they don't have
coronavirus

00:09:26.164 --> 00:09:27.466
should be
an impeachable offense,

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:30.869
because nothing good
ever happens on a cruise ship.

00:09:30.869 --> 00:09:34.606
You never, never once have heard
a positive news story

00:09:34.606 --> 00:09:35.708
about a cruise ship.

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:37.142
You'd never read the headline,

00:09:37.142 --> 00:09:39.411
"Cruise Ship's Toilets
Work Great."

00:09:39.411 --> 00:09:42.180
You have another reminder that
Trump is a lifelong scam artist

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.116
who is constantly running a con

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:46.752
and trying to B.S. his way
out of that con.

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:48.621
It's obvious he doesn't have
a plan for anything

00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:50.322
other than his
own self-preservation.

00:09:50.322 --> 00:09:52.057
For example,
there's been a major delay

00:09:52.057 --> 00:09:54.326
in testing capacity
due to CDC errors,

00:09:54.326 --> 00:09:56.461
which experts have called
a national disgrace.

00:09:56.461 --> 00:09:59.097
Last week, the White House said
it would fail to meet its goal

00:09:59.097 --> 00:10:00.933
in providing
enough coronavirus test kits

00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:02.768
for 1 million people
by the end of the week,

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:04.403
and Vice President
Mike Pence said

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:06.439
they won't have enough tests
to meet demand.

00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:09.241
Then, out of nowhere, during
a visit to the CDC on Friday,

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:11.476
Trump not only said
everyone could get a test,

00:10:11.476 --> 00:10:13.512
he said the tests were perfect,
and for some reason,

00:10:13.512 --> 00:10:15.280
compared them
to his infamous phone call

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.915
with the president of Ukraine,

00:10:16.915 --> 00:10:19.018
you know, the one
that got him impeached.

00:10:19.018 --> 00:10:21.853
-Anybody that wants a test
can get a test.

00:10:21.853 --> 00:10:24.156
Anybody that needs a test
gets a test.

00:10:24.156 --> 00:10:25.858
They're there.
They have the test.

00:10:25.858 --> 00:10:27.759
And the tests are beautiful.

00:10:27.759 --> 00:10:30.396
Anybody that needs a test
gets a test.

00:10:30.396 --> 00:10:34.066
But anybody that needs a test
can have a test.

00:10:34.066 --> 00:10:35.701
They're all set.
They have them out there.

00:10:35.701 --> 00:10:37.603
And the tests are all perfect.

00:10:37.603 --> 00:10:40.305
Like the letter was perfect.

00:10:40.305 --> 00:10:42.741
The transcription was perfect.

00:10:42.741 --> 00:10:44.843
-[ As Trump ] "Anyone who needs
a test gets the test."

00:10:44.843 --> 00:10:46.145
[ Normal voice ]
"I need a test."

